    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problem-solving—something my parents taught me early through puzzles and logic games. Though I never pursued formal education beyond primary school, the structured nature of math aligns with my high conscientiousness and agreeableness traits, making it both challenging yet rewarding. It’s a tool for clarity in everyday life, like measuring distances or calculating budgets.",
